  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Norfenefrine is an alpha-adrenergic agonist, a trace amine also known as meta-octopamine, that has been used as a pharmaceutical drug acting on the cardiovascular system as a cardiac stimulant. It is currently classified as an experimental drug, with no authorised marketing in the European Union, so its present clinical use is unclear.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q12746348&quot;>Wikidata Q12746348</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>norfenefrine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>C01CA05</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13378&quot;>DB13378</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/4538&quot;>4538</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:134779&quot;>134779</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q12746348&quot;>Q12746348</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C8H11NO2</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>153.181 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
